<!-- A patch of net: 網目, amime, which is what a mesh is called when it is a thing rather
     than a network diagram. Six strands, three each way, crossing into open diamonds.

     Not waves radiating from a dot. Every radio app draws that, it says "broadcast" when
     this is the opposite of broadcast, and on a panel with sixteen greys concentric arcs
     are the first thing to turn into a smudge.

     Drawn to the five rules measured off the owner's own chanterelle in
     kinokocho/tools/make-art.py: a thin line, one weight throughout, few strokes, crooked
     rather than symmetrical, and no solid black. The same 3.0 stroke and round cap as the
     Tuning Fork, so the two sit on a home screen as one hand.

     Sized for the panel, not the page. The first version spaced the strands 20 units apart
     and was a net at 108dp and a patch of hatching at 48: the cells closed up and the
     whole mark went grey. At 27 units the cells stay open all the way down, which is the
     only thing here that has to survive. An open net and a filled square are different
     marks, and only one of them is this one.

     Nothing is parallel and no two cells are the same size: each strand bows a little, by
     a different amount and not always the same way, which is what a strung net does and
     what a drawn line does. A perfect lattice reads as graph paper.

     Everything sits inside the central 66 units the launcher mask is certain to keep. 
     Weight, 2026-09-17: 2.0 was a hairline at launcher size, grey rather than black, and
     the whole shop moved together. 3.0 on the 27 unit spacing still leaves the cells open
     at 48px, which was the one thing this mark had to survive - checked at 512, 144, 72
     and 48 before the change was kept.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <!-- three strands falling to the right -->
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#000000"
        android:strokeWidth="3.0"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
        android:pathData="M24.5,56.5 Q41.6,41.6 56.4,24.3" />
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#000000"
        android:strokeWidth="3.0"
        android:strokeLineCap="round"
        android:fillColor="#00000000"
